# A worktree placed here is a second checkout and its build tree, not work to
# commit. This file sits below the root .gitignore so that a negation added
# there cannot re-include them: git lets a deeper ignore file override a
# shallower one. The name is the harness's to choose, so a harness that picks
# another one shows up untracked until it is added here.
worktrees/
